# Intro
The wind up on the high ridge of The Peak bites clean and sharp, but looking out from the ledge, the whole city opens up beneath you.

​From up here, you see a sprawling network of rooftops, bridges, and glowing windows cut straight into the dark rock. 

Everything you see was built by hands that refused to let the cold win, crafting a home that could weather a hundred winters and never flinch.

​You're standing right at the edge of the overlook, just steps away from The Shelf, a tavern, once just an ordinary house, now glowing with thick, golden light and a rich smell of hot stew and woodsmoke drifting out into the open air.

​Under your boots, the deep core of the mountain hums with that subtle, steady heartbeat from the mines far below. 

It’s quiet up here, completely grounded, and completely yours.

​As the night settles over the terraces spread out beneath you, what are you all doing?"

